runed directory is still printed, as a stub'","Design: 'the pass stays inside the Docker root filesystem (find -xdev) and keeps the existing overlay2 cross-device guard'"],"finding":"The design says it 'keeps the existing overlay2 cross-device guard,' but that guard's correctness currently depends on `du -x` pruning at a mount boundary and printing a stub row that a follow-up st_dev comparison overrides (observability.sh:814-835). A `find -xdev` traversal does not descend across devices at all, so the overlay2 subtotal is naturally confined and the stub-override guard is either redundant or must be re-expressed for the new mechanism. The plan does not reconcile this.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdb71dd67a25e825a","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section — 'keeps the existing overlay2 cross-device guard'","norm_id":"n045b4ce8b28223f6","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["overlay2 given its own volume (capacity ticket 5993 remedy)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the back-out mechanism (revert the traversal change) and note the expected one-time step-change in the docker_unaccounted_bytes series so downstream trend/anomaly consumers are not surprised.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'docker_unaccounted_bytes subtracts the Docker ledger from apparent Docker-root bytes' redefines an existing metric","AC4 updates the alarm rationale but no rollback/back-out path or note on historical metric-value discontinuity is stated"],"finding":"The plan changes the semantics/value of an existing published metric (docker_unaccounted_bytes drops ~2.68GiB->1.18GiB) but does not document a back-out mechanism or address the resulting time-series discontinuity for downstream consumers (alarm evaluation history, dashboards, anomaly baselines).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f97e72c60ee501f08","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design / AC4","norm_id":"nda2ea96f1165da1b","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An anomaly/trend baseline computed over the metric's history sees a step change at deploy and mis-fires or masks a real regression","Need to revert if the new computation is wrong in production"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Resolve the 'du-like semantics' capability assertion by specifying the exact hardlink-dedup rule for EACH total and confirming it matches `du` (block mode) and `du --apparent-size` respectively, with the reference du invocations named.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design: 'hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode so allocated/appparent totals retain du-like semantics'","Web (CodeRivers, bootandy/dust#94): `du --apparent-size` does NOT double-count hardlinks but its dedup interaction with logical size differs from block-mode du; 'du-like semantics' is not a single behavior across the two modes"],"finding":"The plan asserts the custom pass de-duplicates hardlinks by device+inode so 'allocated/apparent totals retain du-like semantics', but this capability claim is unverified and diverges from how du actually treats hardlinks under --apparent-size.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0df1af1e3a1f14ca","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (hardlink de-duplication bullet)","norm_id":"n3b33911670591bb9","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The apparent total is expected to match what an operator would get from `du --apparent-size` for cross-checking, but the bespoke dedup rule produces a different number for a Docker root with cross-layer hardlinks"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State in the Design why a bespoke find/stat traversal is preferred over du (e.g. that a single du invocation cannot emit both allocated and apparent totals), so the hand-rolled hardlink-dedup/xdev accounting is a justified reimplementation rather than NIH.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Design: 'one traversal emits all filesystem quantities' and 'This avoids the rejected second du walk from bug 9313'","observability.sh:498-509 comments justify the timeout reduction by there now being 'one walk', i.e. the prior objection was to TWO du walks, not to du","Current impl observability.sh:805 already uses `du -x --block-size=1` which GNU du provides with hardlink dedup and -x pruning built in; the plan re-implements those by hand","GNU du supports --apparent-size for the apparent total and default block accounting — both modes are du-native, though only one per invocation, which the plan does not state as its rationale"],"finding":"The design hand-rolls du-equivalent semantics (hardlink de-dup by device+inode, allocated st_blocks*512, apparent st_size, cross-device pruning) in a bespoke find/stat traversal, without affirmatively establishing why one `du` invocation cannot serve — the cited rejection (bug 9313) is against a SECOND du walk, not against du itself.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fafb73429e4939c1e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (bullets: 'sum of st_blocks*512', 'sum of st_size', 'hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode', 'find -xdev')","norm_id":"nd5d0afb9139d8d88","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/implementer cannot tell whether a stat-accumulator was chosen for a real constraint (du emits one accounting mode per run) or by preference, risking a re-implementation of du's hardlink/xdev edge cases that du already handles correctly"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Justify why a hand-rolled `find -xdev`/stat traversal is chosen over the established `du --apparent-size --block-size=1` mode for the apparent minuend, or adopt du's alternate mode and reconcile it with AC3's 'not two du walks' constraint.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design: 'Replace the Docker-root filesystem census with one metadata pass that returns both sizes: allocated bytes = sum of st_blocks*512 … apparent bytes = sum of st_size'","AC3: 'obtains allocated and apparent Docker-root sizes from one filesystem traversal, not two du walks'","Web (GNU du / CodeRivers, bootandy/dust#94): plain `du` reports allocated blocks and `du --apparent-size` reports the sum of logical st_size — the exact minuend the defect names as the 'commensurable apparent-size residue'","The plan's only prior-art consideration is rejecting 'the rejected second du walk from bug 9313', which addresses walk-count/timeout, not whether du's own --apparent-size mode supplies the apparent total"],"finding":"The Design hand-rolls a `find -xdev` + per-file stat traversal to obtain apparent (st_size) bytes, without considering that the established `du --apparent-size` mode already yields exactly that quantity — so the plan may be reinventing a standard-utility capability rather than reusing it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5402851360af0d6f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (single metadata pass); AC3","norm_id":"na1915b972df1c243","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer builds a custom stat-accumulating traversal that must independently re-derive du's block-rounding, sparse-file, and cross-device behavior instead of passing a flag to the tool the current code already invokes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Note in the Design that GNU `du --apparent-size --block-size=1` yields the st_size sum directly; state whether the apparent total will come from that mode (and whether AC3's one-traversal goal is met by a single du invocation, an alternate-mode du, or a genuinely necessary custom pass), and record why the chosen option beats reusing du.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the exact traversal mechanism and verify its flags against the deploy host (e.g. GNU `find -xdev -printf '%b %s %D %i\\n'` for allocated/apparent/device/inode), or state the `stat`-based fallback, so AC3's single-pass allocated+apparent+hardlink-dedup claim is grounded rather than assumed.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7845,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Design: 'Replace the Docker-root filesystem census with one metadata pass that returns both sizes ... the pass stays inside the Docker root filesystem (`find -xdev`)'","Current census uses `du -x --block-size=1 --max-depth=1` (observability.sh:805), not find -printf; the field codes %b (512-block allocated) and %s (apparent) are GNU-findutils extensions, unverified against the target host's find implementation","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — the tools exist and the technique is achievable on GNU coreutils, but the specific flag surface the 'single pass' depends on is unnamed and unconfirmed for the deploy environment"],"finding":"The Design asserts a single `find -xdev` pass emits both allocated (st_blocks*512) and apparent (st_size) totals with device+inode hardlink de-dup, but never names the concrete mechanism (e.g. `find -printf '%b %s %D %i'` vs invoking `stat` per file). `%b`/`%s`/`%D`/`%i` are GNU-findutils-specific printf directives, not POSIX; on a BusyBox or minimal `find` they are absent, which would falsify the 'one traversal' claim. The current script deliberately uses `du`/`stat` rather than `find -printf`, so this is a not-before-used capability for this probe and its flag-level surface is Partially-verified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f21f33ccb67ca7db8","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (\"one metadata pass that returns both sizes\"; `find -xdev`)","norm_id":"n72c8ce03e0cfd672","priority":0.1155,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Target host ships BusyBox find or a find lacking -printf %b/%s, so the single-pass design silently cannot produce allocated+apparent from one traversal and AC3 becomes unachievable as written","Implementer picks per-file `stat` fork-per-file over the whole Docker root, reintroducing the O(files) cost the bug-9313 single-walk constraint was meant to avoid"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artif